PS5 VRR test 28: Sony's timing SDP and the chip's follow mode (Lawson)  [ps5-bazzite-deck]

Ported from Lawson's PS5 VRR work (kernel vrr13, 28 Oct: real VRR, the TV's FreeSync
following the game). Only with hdmi.vrr_test=1 on FLAVA3, follow mode with
hdmi.vrr_chip=2; nothing changes otherwise.
 - amdgpu: Sony's GPU VRR packet, a DP extension SDP (HB 39 04) with the source timing
   (h_total, h_start, h_sync, v_start, v_sync; DB10 = 1), every frame from the
   adaptive-sync slot while VRR is active; instead of the FreeSync SDP by default
   (hdmi.vrr_timing_sdp=1, 2 = both, 0 = off)
 - DC: DPCD 0x107 MSA_TIMING_PAR_IGNORE_EN stays clear on the chip, which drops its
   input lock when it's set, while the GPU still varies the frame length (DRR)
   (hdmi.vrr_sink_msa=1 restores the bit)
 - hdmi: vrr_chip=2 keeps the setup normal and switches the chip to follow mode only
   after the SDP flows: a FreeSync SPD (40 Hz .. mode refresh) in the SPD slot 0x7240,
   then 0x6064=03, 0x1047=30, 0x600c=01 00, 0x6224=40 0f, 0x6c07=80, one per
   hdmi.vrr_follow_ms (1000); vrr_chip is a number now (0/1 as before)
